"836","(the wife of the Prophet) I told Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) that Safiya bint Huyai had got her menses. He said, She will probably delay us. Did she perform Tawaf (Al-Ifada) with you?"" We replied"
"837","Safiya got her menses on the night of Nafr (departure from Hajj), and she said, I see that I will detain you."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said"
"838","This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Ibn Juraij with the same chain of transmitters. And the narration of Ibn Bakr is like one transmitted by 'Isa but with this (variation): There are not these words in it: To all these three rites (throwing of pebbles sacrificing of animal and shaving of one's head)."" And so far as the narration of Yahya al-Umawi (the words are): I got (my head) shaved before I sacrificed the animal"
"839","Narrated lbn 'Abbis u{j, dJriJ When the Prophett *r.*.l entered the Ka'ba, he invoked Allah in each and every side of it and did not offe Saldt (praver) till he came out of it aftcoming out he offered a twof Rak'a prayfacing the Ka'ba and said, This is the Qiblah"""
"840","`Abdullah bin Abu `Aufa said: Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) performed `Umra and we too performed `Umra along with him. When he entered Mecca he performed the Tawaf (of Ka`ba) and we too performed it along with him"
"841","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said to me, Were your people not close to the Pre-Islamic period of ignorance"
"842","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) called the salamander a bad animal, but I did not hear him ordering it to be killed."""
"843","I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about the wall (outside the Ka`ba). Is it regarded as part of the Ka`ba?"" He replied"
"844","Al Fadl was riding behind the Prophet (ﷺ) and a woman from the tribe of Khath'am came up. Al Fadl started looking at her and she looked at him. The Prophet (ﷺ) turned Al-Fadl's face to the other side. She said, My father has come under Allah's obligation of performing Hajj but he is very old man and cannot sit properly on his Rahila (mount). Shall I perform Hajj on his behalf ? The Prophet (ﷺ) replied affirmative. That happened during Hajjat-ul-Wada' of the Prophet (ﷺ)."""
"845","A womand from the tribe of Khath'am came in the yeare (of Hajjat-al-Wadd' of the Prophett .r:r,, d-r, *b) and said, O Allah' Messenger"
"846","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Allah created Adam in His picture"
"847","The Prophett J-r..r, d,r; said, A womand should not travel fmore thand three days except with a Dhfi- Mahram (i.e. a male with whom she cannot marry at all"
"848","Abu Sa`id who participated in twelve Ghazawat with the Prophet (ﷺ) said, I heard four things from Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) (or I narrate them from the Prophet (ﷺ) ) which won my admiration and appreciation. They are: -1. ""No lady should travel without her husband or without a Dhu-Mahram for a two-days' journey. -2. No fasting is permissible on two days of `Id-ul-Fitr"
"849","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, It is not lawful for a lady who believes in Allah and the Last Day"
